WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:10.597
ago Alligator stayed in the river during the daytime.

2
00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:15.960
While the sun shone, he swam and rested in the cool water.

3
00:00:16.821 --> 00:00:21.523
Only at night did Alligator climb out, letting moonlight wash over him.

4
00:00:23.444 --> 00:00:26.226
One night Frog hopped closer and stared.

5
00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:30.248
"Why, Alligator, you glow in the moonlight!"

6
00:00:30.924 --> 00:00:32.866
Turtle lifted his head and nodded.

7
00:00:32.886 --> 00:00:37.630
"The skin on your back is so smooth and golden!"

8
00:00:38.911 --> 00:00:40.992
Alligator puffed up with pride.

9
00:00:41.012 --> 00:00:42.834
"Thank you, friends."

10
00:00:43.935 --> 00:00:47.498
Their praise warmed him more than moonlight ever had.

11
00:00:47.518 --> 00:00:53.363
The next day Alligator remembered their glowing words and admiring eyes.

12
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:57.126
"I felt so important," he thought.

13
00:00:57.146 --> 00:00:59.448
"Like the king of the river!

14
00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:02.717
So why should I hide my beauty in darkness?

15
00:01:03.478 --> 00:01:05.439
Everyone should see me clearly."

16
00:01:06.459 --> 00:01:11.702
And so, when the sun next rose, Alligator crawled onto the riverbank.

17
00:01:11.722 --> 00:01:13.543
"Good morning!

18
00:01:14.104 --> 00:01:17.305
Come see me—your golden king!"

19
00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:22.168
"Alligator!" Frog hurried over.

20
00:01:22.188 --> 00:01:24.489
"The sun is strong!

21
00:01:25.029 --> 00:01:26.430
It might burn your back."

22
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.552
Alligator laughed and flicked his tail.

23
00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:32.910
"I'm much stronger than the sun!"

24
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:37.212
Along the river animals gathered, whispering and pointing.

25
00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:41.856
"The skin on his back shines," Turtle said.

26
00:01:42.556 --> 00:01:43.317
Otter nodded.

27
00:01:43.337 --> 00:01:45.798
"He looks so powerful."

28
00:01:45.818 --> 00:01:48.560
"Like a river king!"

29
00:01:49.201 --> 00:01:49.881
Fish said.

30
00:01:50.742 --> 00:01:51.802
Alligator grinned.

31
00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:54.224
"Move aside, Otter!

32
00:01:54.965 --> 00:01:56.986
You're blocking everyone's view."

33
00:01:58.047 --> 00:01:59.508
He swung toward Beaver.

34
00:02:00.268 --> 00:02:02.289
"Bring me more food—now!"

35
00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:07.511
High above, Vulture circled the riverbank.

36
00:02:09.132 --> 00:02:13.694
He watched as animals scurried about, obeying Alligator's orders.

37
00:02:15.194 --> 00:02:18.096
He listened as Alligator bragged loudly.

38
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:21.157
Finally Vulture flew down.

39
00:02:21.177 --> 00:02:24.318
"Pride grows heavy, Alligator.

40
00:02:25.059 --> 00:02:27.780
It can weigh down even the strongest creature."

41
00:02:29.096 --> 00:02:31.697
Alligator scoffed and waved his tail.

42
00:02:32.378 --> 00:02:34.098
"You envy me, Vulture.

43
00:02:34.759 --> 00:02:37.080
Now fly away and leave me to my glory!"

44
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.402
He stretched across the hot riverbank and fell asleep.

45
00:02:43.822 --> 00:02:47.304
When he woke, his skin stung and felt tight.

46
00:02:47.324 --> 00:02:50.105
"Ouch!" he thought.

47
00:02:51.506 --> 00:02:53.126
Still, he laughed loudly.

48
00:02:53.146 --> 00:02:56.508
"What a fine nap for a fine king!"

49
00:02:57.724 --> 00:03:01.125
Each day Alligator returned to the sunny riverbank.

50
00:03:01.965 --> 00:03:05.206
Each day his skin grew tighter and drier.

51
00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.667
Soon the others began to hide from him.

52
00:03:09.687 --> 00:03:12.908
"He's so bossy," Frog said.

53
00:03:13.528 --> 00:03:14.409
Turtle nodded.

54
00:03:14.429 --> 00:03:16.569
"He brags too much."

55
00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.970
One morning Frog stared.

56
00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.551
"Something's wrong."

57
00:03:22.571 --> 00:03:25.312
"Alligator's skin is cracking!"

58
00:03:25.792 --> 00:03:26.632
Turtle cried.

59
00:03:27.632 --> 00:03:28.932
Indeed, it was true.

60
00:03:29.913 --> 00:03:32.974
Alligator's golden smoothness was gone.

61
00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:38.475
Now ridges, bumps, and deep lines covered his back.

62
00:03:39.436 --> 00:03:40.716
Vulture flew down.

63
00:03:40.736 --> 00:03:44.137
"Nothing shines forever, Alligator.

64
00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.938
Especially too much pride."

65
00:03:48.118 --> 00:03:50.079
Shame filled Alligator's heart.

66
00:03:50.999 --> 00:03:53.620
Slowly he slid back into the river.

67
00:03:55.213 --> 00:03:58.416
"I ruined everything," he thought.

68
00:03:59.578 --> 00:04:03.182
To this day, Alligator stays mostly hidden from others.

69
00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:07.287
Only his eyes and nose appear above the water.

70
00:04:08.108 --> 00:04:11.032
And forever, his back remains rough.
